venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
config/dev.ini
config/prod.ini
logs/*.log
.bin/
uploads/
test_tone.wav

# NOT migrations/. Every teammate's database is built by `flask db upgrade`,
# so a migration that stays out of the repository is a schema change nobody
# else can apply: they pull code that queries a column their database has
# never been given, and every request touching that table 500s. That is
# exactly how b8f3c21d90ae (users.username, password_reset_tokens) went
# missing and broke sign-in for everyone but the machine it was written on.
# Only the compiled cache is ignored, by the __pycache__ rule above.
